My vote is that no named weapons or wands of wishing should be
created by a wand of polymorph.  Here's why:

Named weapons are usually gifts from the gods, and polymorphing
piles of weapons has nothing to do with the gods.  Getting named
weapons from polymorphing seems inappropriate to the game.

Wands of wishing should only be found by the lucky, and not created
by the devious.  If I have a wand of polymorph and then find a shop
with 15 or so wands, it is virtually a won game.  (This happened to
me this morning, but after I had my first wand of wishing a Balrog happened
to appear and killed me.  This is no great loss since there is no sport
in such a game.)  Also, if a player makes it down to find the wand of
wishing he can without fail make himself invincible given a little time.

The other day I got the wand of wishing and soon found myself with
great armor, excellent weapons, 6 amulets of lifesaving, and 3 extra
wands of wishing to use to create cockatrice corpses everytime the
wiz showed up.  Not a very satisfying way to win a game.  But this is
available to every player who gets the wand of wishing and knows how.
(Yes, even in patchlevel 6.)  It seems that after you get to the point
where you find the wand of wishing, the game is over if you want it
to be.  This did take a fair amount of time, but it payed off when I
got to the mazes and was able to map each one.  Then I could just
teleport to the stairs and avoid the frustrations of wandering around
23 mazes.  (This is why the compass idea is such a good one.)

What fun is the game if you can be invincible?

One answer is to show a little restraint and not abuse the wand of
polymorph like this.  It seems a little silly, though, to not use
all the techniques a game has to offer.  So, to avoid having the game
be a won game for those who get the wand of wishing, I propose that
the game be changed so that wands of wishing cannot be created by
polymorphing.  With this the game is to be won by meeting the challenges
of the dungeon, and not by persistence with polymorphing.

I would leave open the possibility of getting magic lamps thru polymorph,
but I would change it.  Currently, after you get a lamp and make the wish
you can throw it back on the pile and polymorph until it becomes another
magic lamp, fully recharged.  If the new lamp were also spent, then
polymorphing piles of tools would not create enough wishes to tempt even
the most persistent polymorphers on for so long.  Make sure that spent
lamps polymorph into spent lamps.

With these two changes it would probably be impossible to become invincible
thru polymorphing piles.  On the other hand, polymorphing would still be
powerful enough so that you could create most of the things that you need
to survive the mazes.


